     full-shape fixture, but issued as a CORRECTION — BT-3 InvoiceTypeCode is
     384 (Corrected invoice, UNTDID 1001) instead of 380 (Commercial invoice).

     WHY 384 NEEDS A PRECEDING-INVOICE REFERENCE:
       XRechnung rule BR-DE-26 requires that when BT-3 is 384 the invoice MUST
       carry a PRECEDING INVOICE REFERENCE (BG-3): the identifier of the invoice
       this document corrects. This fixture supplies it via
       cac:BillingReference/cac:InvoiceDocumentReference with a Preceding Invoice
       reference (BT-25) plus its issue date (BT-26), so BR-DE-26 is SATISFIED
       and the invoice validates CLEAN. Its negative twin
       (synth-ubl-bad-corrected_ubl.xml) drops that reference to make BR-DE-26
       fire — BR-DE-26 is only a WARNING, so the twin stays valid=true.

     ARITHMETIC (identical to synth-ubl-good-fullshape, all EUR, consistent):
       line 1 (19%): 10 x 50.00 = 500.00 - 20.00 line allowance -> BT-131 = 480.00
       line 2 (19%):  4 x 30.00 = 120.00                         -> BT-131 = 120.00
       line 3 ( 7%):  5 x 22.00 = 110.00 + 10.00 line charge     -> BT-131 = 120.00
       line 4 ( 7%):  2 x 40.00 =  80.00                         -> BT-131 =  80.00
       BT-106 sum of line nets = 800.00; doc allowance 50.00 (19%), doc charge
       30.00 (7%); 19% base 550.00 -> VAT 104.50; 7% base 230.00 -> VAT 16.10;
       BT-109 = 780.00; BT-110 = 120.60; BT-112 = BT-115 = 900.60 -->
